auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Agenda Buddy — local API collection

  See `README.md` in this folder for the same content in a form you can read without opening Bruno
  (GitHub, a file browser, etc.) — including why an error response is JSON, not HTML, and what to do if
  you still see HTML somewhere.

  As of **F-015 (v0.5.0)** every request outside `7-Health` goes through the **Gateway** at
  `{{gatewayUrl}}` — the same `api/v1/{service}/**` allowlist `MobileApp` uses, forwarded byte-for-byte
  with no path rewriting. `7-Health` is the one exception: `/health` and `/alive` are not in the
  Gateway's allowlist by design (T-302), so each service's health still has to be checked directly
  against its own `*Url` variable — that's the only place those seven per-service variables are still
  used.

  ## Read this first: run `0-Auth/2 Login` before anything else

  As of **F-016 (v0.2.0)** nearly every route requires a JWT. Without a token you will get `401` on
  everything except the two `Profession` reads. `0-Auth/1 Register` and `0-Auth/2 Login` both capture
  `accessToken` and `refreshToken` into the active environment automatically, and this collection sends
  `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` on every request.

  Register a **Provider** first: `2-Customer/List customers` and `1-Provider/Create provider` both
  require the `Provider` role, and a `Customer`-role token gets `403` on them by design.

  ## Which environment to pick

  - **Local (standalone)** — fixed ports from each service's `appsettings.json` for the seven `*Url`
    (health-check) variables: `dotnet run --project AgendaBuddy.Provider.Api --no-launch-profile`, etc.
    Application requests still need the Gateway; use the AppHost environment for those.
  - **Local (Aspire AppHost)** — `dotnet run --project AgendaBuddy.AppHost` starts everything, but
    the Gateway's local host address is pinned to `http://localhost:6080`. Only the seven direct service
    ports are dynamic; fill their `*Url` variables from the dashboard if you need `7-Health`. Also note:
    Aspire does **not** run the services as `Development`, so Swagger UI is unavailable there.

  ## Regenerating the OpenAPI specs

      REGENERATE_OPENAPI_BASELINES=1 dotnet test AgendaBuddy.IntegrationTests \
        /p:MobileWorkloads=false --filter FullyQualifiedName~OpenApiSpecBaselineWriter

  That command writes the committed, byte-deterministic baselines. `./scripts/generate-openapi.sh` remains
  useful for reading live specs or refreshing `index.md`, but it formats JSON differently and must not be
  used to regenerate the committed baseline files.
}
